From 6410eae36353cb597893837be810b3632631f0c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Matti=20Lehtim=C3=A4ki?= <matti.lehtimaki@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Jan 2023 18:34:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 21/43] remoteproc: qcom_wcnss: Add qcom,wcn3660a compatible
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WCN3660A is a variant of WCN3660, but with the same regulator
requirements as WCN3620/WCN3680/WCN3660B. As far as qcom_wcnss_iris
is concerned we can just use qcom,wcn3680 (wcn3680_data).

However, a separate compatible is needed for WCN3660A because
the wcn36xx driver uses it to enable chip-specific functionality.
In particular, it enables 802.11ac for qcom,wcn3680 which is not
supported by WCN3660A.

Signed-off-by: Matti Lehtimäki <matti.lehtimaki@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 5a913a2171d19ed8f40b2060cfb68ef782cd3e8d)
---
