From: Luca Weiss <luca@z3ntu.xyz>
Date: Tue, 23 Apr 2024 22:45:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 34/43] HACK soc: qcom: mdt_loader: Make wcnss boot on
 htc-memul

[ 50.511358] qcom-wcnss-pil fb204000.remoteproc: overriding hash_size for msm8926-htc-memul wcnss old=0x168 new=0x1a68!

If you remove a byte from hash_size, then it also doesn't work it
seems.. Funky behavior..

(cherry picked from commit a7f6776eba95c7e1982566e3ac70ebeae2ad31e0)
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/mdt_loader.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/mdt_loader.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/mdt_loader.c
index 002100fe2d32..01cd525e49ea 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/mdt_loader.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/mdt_loader.c
@@ -198,6 +198,12 @@ void *qcom_mdt_read_metadata(const struct firmware *fw, size_t *data_len,
 	ehdr_size = phdrs[0].p_filesz;
 	hash_size = phdrs[hash_segment].p_filesz;
 
+	if (strcmp(fw_name, "qcom/msm8926/memul/wcnss.mdt") == 0) {
+		dev_warn(dev, "overriding hash_size for msm8926-htc-memul wcnss old=0x%x new=0x%x!\n", hash_size, fw->size - ehdr_size);
+		// Set hash_size to the remaining part of the loaded firmware file (fw->size == ehdr_size + hash_size)
+		hash_size = fw->size - ehdr_size;
+	}
+
 	data = kmalloc(ehdr_size + hash_size, GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!data)
 		return ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM);
-- 
