From 3dfa9b7dc85ea74760f0e7736bf7b6a9875b36ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luca Weiss <luca@lucaweiss.eu>
Date: Wed, 1 Apr 2026 18:06:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 39/43] mailbox: Print mbox parse failure details on error

When of_parse_phandle_with_args fails, expand the error message with
some useful information.

I'd argue that this error print shouldn't even exist in the first place,
the caller should be responsible for handling the error and printing an
error message if appropriate. For example in drivers/soc/qcom/smsm.c
mbox_request_channel() is preferred with a fallback to
syscon_node_to_regmap(), depending if the devicetree was updated.

Signed-off-by: Luca Weiss <luca@lucaweiss.eu>
(cherry picked from commit 16fcad8334b7fdacfe1efd4fc652fdc5e73f09bb)
---
 drivers/mailbox/mailbox.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mailbox/mailbox.c b/drivers/mailbox/mailbox.c
index efacd24a085d..9f217bd1bd3b 100644
--- a/drivers/mailbox/mailbox.c
+++ b/drivers/mailbox/mailbox.c
@@ -451,7 +451,7 @@ struct mbox_chan *mbox_request_channel(struct mbox_client *cl, int index)
 	ret = fwnode_property_get_reference_args(fwnode, "mboxes", "#mbox-cells",
 						 0, index, &fwspec);
 	if (ret) {
-		dev_err(dev, "%s: can't parse \"%s\" property\n", __func__, "mboxes");
+		dev_err(dev, "%s: can't parse \"mboxes\" property for index %d: %d\n", __func__, index, ret);
 		return ERR_PTR(ret);
 	}
 
-- 
2.56.1


From f2b90ac85ca6460f5ea3ec23db2f5cdc00685cd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
